{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558666107,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf86ad3ffe7OMdIoF41pRkUC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40824b6001w3LrpKeBIzm3eS","sessionID":"ses_e2bf86ad3ffe7OMdIoF41pRkUC","messageID":"msg_1d408175c001KiKBSIAZcW8vst","type":"tool","id":"call_00_24tqb4gyok1jmg2wnp8ta9ng","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"45\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26:`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:162:With `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=true`, `skill_graph_scan` also harvests frontmatter (`title`, `description`, `trigger_phrases`, `importance_tier`, `contextType`) from every markdown file under each skill's `references/` and `assets/` (READMEs excluded) into a `skill_docs` table. The watcher registers those docs so edits re-index the owning skill. Doc phrases score inside the `derived_generated` lane: top-3 docs per skill, tier-weighted, contribution capped at 0.45, so they assist ranking but cannot hard-route alone. Matching recommendations carry an optional `matchedDocs` field (max 3 sanitized skill-relative paths) pointing at the exact doc to open.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 45 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26:`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:162:With `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=true`, `skill_graph_scan` also harvests frontmatter (`title`, `description`, `trigger_phrases`, `importance_tier`, `contextType`) from every markdown file under each skill's `references/` and `assets/` (READMEs excluded) into a `skill_docs` table. The watcher registers those docs so edits re-index the owning skill. Doc phrases score inside the `derived_generated` lane: top-3 docs per skill, tier-weighted, contribution capped at 0.45, so they assist ranking but cannot hard-route alone. Matching recommendations carry an optional `matchedDocs` field (max 3 sanitized skill-relative paths) pointing at the exact doc to open.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 45 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"45\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558665910,"end":1794558666107}}}}
