{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558671039,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf86ad3ffe7OMdIoF41pRkUC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d408380f0015AceRy00xZksCm","sessionID":"ses_e2bf86ad3ffe7OMdIoF41pRkUC","messageID":"msg_1d4082a1f001xAzXtBmjc5BKRy","type":"tool","id":"call_01_64ujwclkwqaumjwkwl2y3m1r","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 46 rows in all.","oldString":"`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all.","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n@@ -22,9 +22,9 @@\n ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n \n ### Command Vectors\n \n-`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n+`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 46 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n \n `skill_graph_scan` embeds that text into a separate `vec_cmd_<dim>` table. The table carries no foreign key, and the skill vector table is left untouched. A row whose text hash has not changed is skipped. A stored row that the deriver no longer generates is pruned.\n \n ### Passing on Meaning\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 46 rows in all.\", \"oldString\": \"`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 45 rows in all.\", \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558670863,"end":1794558671039}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558671043,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf86ad3ffe7OMdIoF41pRkUC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40837be001XegqC2nihItZ2l","sessionID":"ses_e2bf86ad3ffe7OMdIoF41pRkUC","messageID":"msg_1d4082a1f001xAzXtBmjc5BKRy","type":"tool","id":"call_00_pwqyclstijnrlndkt3e2s81r","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves","oldString":"The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 45 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n@@ -172,9 +172,9 @@\n ### The Embedder\n \n The `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n \n-Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 45 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n+Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n \n ### The Nine Commands\n \n The CLI exposes nine commands, each accepting snake case, kebab case and camel case spellings. `list-tools` enumerates all nine. `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` is only trust-gated for the mutating apply path. Report, propose, dry-run apply stay read-safe. You have already met the first three in Quick Start.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves\", \"oldString\": \"The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 45 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves\", \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558670782,"end":1794558671043}}}}
